r":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T10:20:28-08:00","id":805328,"title":"","content":"Following my previous post in this thread, I share two of the most comical Heroes I've seen in a long time: the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SOuNeX9kmWw\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Starbarians</b></a> (NSFW: profanity, violence, nudity and sex).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:21:31-08:00","id":808936,"title":"","content":"I wish so much to do a Silent Hill based game, it was the first thing I thought of reading the blurb on the site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T12:50:52-08:00","id":821143,"title":"","content":"I've found that Bloodborne is ripe with inspiration for Beast, both visually and thematically. Aside from some quite awesome Horrors and the whole &quot;Hunters VS Beasts&quot; thing, the game explores some concepts that, if not exactly related to Beast, come from a similar neighborood. Nightmares, dark hungers and primeval supernatural lineages are all there and, even if Bloodborne goes a completely different road which has more to do with Lovecraft's Cthulhu Mythos and Dream cycle, it still offers plenty of ideas, eye candy and plot hooks for Beast.<br /> <br /> P.S. Sure, many bosses and areas from the Souls series offer easy inspiration for Horrors and Lairs, but Bloodborne goes even further, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-01-2016, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:00:20-08:00","id":821227,"title":"","content":"A recent film I saw called the Drownsman has a very good look at a Lair, and nice atmospherics for merging it with the world. (The acting's a but rudimentary though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T22:44:03-08:00","id":823086,"title":"","content":"Although best known for her <i>Night World</i> series, L.J. Smith's <b>Forbidden Game</b> trilogy has a lot of potential for a <i>Beast</i> game. The antagonist, Julian, reads a bit more fae than Begotten . . . but many of the setting elements work perfectly with the Beast framework.<br /> <br /> Take the first book, <b>The Hunter</b>, for example. A high school senior, looking for something different for her next big party, picks up &quot;The Game&quot; at a mysterious store. The game board is &quot;The House&quot;, and each player has to decorate a room to resemble their worst nightmare. As the clock strikes nine, all the friends pass out . . . only to wake up inside an apparently real version of The House. <br /> <br /> And The House really does resemble a Beast's Lair. The windows in the main part of the building look out onto primal chaos, for one thing. And each room resembles a Chamber. One room is an alien abduction scene, another is the ultimate messy room (complete with earthquake and screaming fungus), a third is the basement of a relative's house . . . And if the protagonist wants to rescue her friends, she'll have to find each one in their room - and then find the Burrow leading back to the House (and the clock is ticking).<br /> <br /> The second book really reads <b>Changeling</b> to me, but the third has a nice example of using magic to intrude on a Beast's Lair. And since the protagonist is familiar with the area it was based on, it gives some ideas on how a Chamber might differ from its real world inspiration. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T09:43:05-07:00","id":873140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vKFDpI9ihLs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vKFDpI9ihLs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vKFDpI9ihLs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vKFDpI9ihLs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Sandman. A short animated film, which made an impression of a seven-year-old me. It's Ugallu inspiration, all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5260-themangynimrod","name":"TheMangyNimrod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:22:21-07:00","id":873163,"title":"","content":"This seems so obvious that I'm sure it must have been said before, but what about Batman? The whole point of his persona is to strike primeval fear into the hearts of criminals. He sure as hell hungers for punishment, has a lair, and I've never really bought that his cape could let him glide like he does...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T18:55:14-07:00","id":879838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/595179-beast-inspiration?p=873163#post873163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems so obvious that I'm sure it must have been said before, but what about Batman? The whole point of his persona is to strike primeval fear into the hearts of criminals. He sure as hell hungers for punishment, has a lair, and I've never really bought that his cape could let him glide like he does...</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/660807-batman-ugallu-nemesis\"><b>This has been brought up before</b></a>, and I agree. I prefer to think of him an as Ugallu.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T00:27:48-07:00","id":879953,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna say this is an Anakim<br /> <a href=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/89d42f94e913f304017eca66b7ed7a93/tumblr_mmi76lwoWG1s3tm36o9_r1_1280.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://41.media.tumblr.com/89d42f94e...o9_r1_1280.jpg</a><br /> <br /> This is a Namtaru<br /> <a href=\"https://cdn1.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/000/218/141/large/adrian-smith-monster7envyfin.jpg?1443928015\" target=\"_blank\">https://cdn1.artstation.com/p/assets...jpg?1443928015</a><br /> <br /> Also this is a Namtaru<br /> <a href=\"https://cdn0.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/000/218/908/large/adrian-smith-spawn.jpg?1443927632\" target=\"_blank\">https://cdn0.artstation.com/p/assets...jpg?1443927632</a><br /> <br /> This is an Anakim, but considering it looks like it's bursting out of a volcano or mountain where it's been for ages I could also see an argument for the least indicative Makara around<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://digital-art-gallery.com/picture/big/12803\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://digital-art-gallery.com/site/static/common/build/images/flag_codes/us.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://digital-art-gallery.com/picture/big/12803\" target=\"_blank\"> Digital Art Gallery Online / 20 627 pictures and photos </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://digital-art-gallery.com/picture/big/12803\" target=\"_blank\"> http://digital-art-gallery.com/picture/big/12803 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I saw this and my immediate thought is this is a Beast trying to wake up it's Tyrant Horror from a food coma<br /> \u200b<a href=\"http://www.art-spire.com/wp-content/gallery/2014/Aout_2014/22-08-14_Xiaodi_Jin/Xiaodi_Jin_07.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.art-spire.com/wp-content/...odi_Jin_07.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"us