itle":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:42:06-07:00","id":880367,"title":"","content":"Lovecraft's <a href=\"http://www.dagonbytes.com/thelibrary/lovecraft/theoutsider.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>&quot;The Outsider&quot;</b></a> is a perfect example of the Devouring/Homecoming, probably of a Namtaru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T18:21:42-07:00","id":912560,"title":"","content":"Hogfather by Terry Pratchett has some interesting similarities. The original Bogeyman turned Tooth Fairy is an example of a monster that cares. And Mr. Teatime, while more of a Slasher than a Hero, would be a very, very upsetting sort of Hero to encounter in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T03:20:05-07:00","id":912715,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\">It's <span style=\"font-family:arial\">pronounced &quot;Teh-ah</span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-tim-eh&quot;.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T12:30:29-07:00","id":912929,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1lxsMHeOGjE\" target=\"_blank\">Going Under the Bed</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T16:08:13-07:00","id":932241,"title":"","content":"(I'm not sure if thread necromancy is a rule on Onyx Path boards - if so and a mod sees this please feel free to split into a new thread)<br /> <br /> So I've spent the last few days checking out the Beast movies recommended in the core book, and it's been an interesting experience I thought I would share.Here are my opinions in watching order:<br /> <br /> <b>Tucker &amp; Dale vs Evil: </b>I like this one, although I feel it could have been even better. It's very well done, just thought it could have done with a few extra laughs and twists. The main romance felt a bit too &quot;good guy gets the girl as a prize&quot; to me. But to me the Beast value definitely was in the bad guy. Like the core book says, he's a very interesting example of Hero attitude. I won't say much more to avoid spoilers, but his relationship with the main characters is very reminiscent of the Beast/Hero connection.<br /> <br /> <b>Feast: </b>That one I felt about in the opposite way: I quite liked the story and content, but it could clearly have used some better production values (I'm conscious it was made on a low budget, however). The small profiles on screen had me laugh out loud a few times (special mention for the Life Expectancy of the Vet). Beast value is... I'm not sure what it is? The main characters don't feel like Heroes, and the monsters are as basic as can be. I think perhaps the interest is in how people in the movie actually react to extreme situations as people, and NOT as movie heroes.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightbreed </b>(two hours, blue ray Cabal cut): OK, that movie was like a revelation to me and clearly the &quot;Beast-est&quot; of all the ones I watched. The society of disparate monsters, who run the gamut from &quot;Mindless killers and cannibals&quot; to &quot;people who just want to raise their children and pets in peace&quot;, was oddly touching to me. I guess I just felt a connection with the &quot;freaks&quot;, and I feel a lot of people will too. Plus in a way the Nightbreed induct new members through a Devouring of their own. The sheriff and therapist (played by David Cronenberg - how's that for horror cred??) are also good examples of Heroes, who seem to gather followers way too easy, as if people were just looking for an excuse to shoot things. If you haven't seen it I highly recommend it. <br /> <br /> Bonus round!<br /> <br /> High on Clive Barker's work I decided to check out <b>Candyman</b>, and I really enjoyed it as well. I was surprised at both the setting - the Chicago projects - and the main protagonist, a non-victimized woman.Plus the movie plays a lot with notions of legends, fear, and consequences, such that I felt it actually was a really good fit for Beast. Candyman himself and his relationship with bees seem like a perfect example of the Infestation Atavism.The ending I won't spoil but exemplifies another key Beast concept to me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks to the Beast authors for listing these - movies I might never have watched had they not been mentioned. I might need to dig into the other core books for other recommendations!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T02:09:06-07:00","id":935996,"title":"","content":"Tsukihime they have a weapon designed with the horn of a unicorn in it to counter reincarnation. A unicorn horn is used because in that setting <b>Unicorns are believed to eat souls.</b> To quote the wiki on the weapon <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Type Moon Wikia: Seventh Scripture</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Created by felling a Unicorn, a beast said to consume souls, they used its horn as a key,</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T11:32:40-07:00","id":937704,"title":"","content":"Was just thinking Diana from Lights Out might make a Decent Beast... I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin